WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.169
AI governance is the set of roles, policies, processes, decisions, and oversight mechanisms an organization uses to manage AI responsibly.

2
00:00:09.169 --> 00:00:11.804
It helps teams answer practical questions.

3
00:00:11.804 --> 00:00:13.550
Which AI systems are we using?

4
00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:14.488
Who owns them?

5
00:00:14.488 --> 00:00:16.025
What data do they process?

6
00:00:16.025 --> 00:00:17.652
What risks do they create?

7
00:00:17.652 --> 00:00:19.049
How are they evaluated?

8
00:00:19.049 --> 00:00:29.306
Governance also clarifies who approves higher-risk uses, how issues are monitored, and how concerns are addressed when the system changes or behaves unexpectedly.

9
00:00:29.306 --> 00:00:32.609
Good governance does not exist to stop useful AI work.

10
00:00:32.609 --> 00:00:36.919
It exists to make AI use visible, accountable, risk-aware, and manageable.
